fix-response-code-positions: number handle and parameter response codes per Part 3

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "Response Code Formats" (Table:
Format-One Response Codes (TPM_RC))):

  "When an error is associated with a parameter, TPM_RC_P (0x040) is added
  and N is set to the parameter number. ... For an error associated with a
  handle, a parameter number (1 to 7) is added to the N field. For an error
  associated with a session, a value of 8 plus the session number (1 to 7)
  is added to the N field."

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "Response Code Formats" (Note)):

  "In the Reference Code, for a RC_FMT1 response code, a constant of the
  form RC_Command_parameterName is the one based parameter number (TPM_RC_n)
  plus TPM_RC_P."

Response-code positions follow the Part 3 command layout: handles are
TPM_RC_H + n and parameters TPM_RC_P + n counted after the handles. Seven
command headers (ACT_SetTimeout, ChangePPS, ContextSave, HierarchyChangeAuth,
NV_ReadPublic, PolicyGetDigest, SequenceUpdate) number them wrongly.

diff --git a/src/ChangePPS_fp.h b/src/ChangePPS_fp.h
--- a/src/ChangePPS_fp.h
+++ b/src/ChangePPS_fp.h
@@ -68,7 +68,10 @@ typedef struct {
     TPMI_RH_PLATFORM	authHandle;
 } ChangePPS_In;
 
-#define RC_ChangePPS_authHandle	(TPM_RC_P + TPM_RC_1)
+// tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+// response-code positions per the Part 3 command layout (handles are
+// TPM_RC_H + n, parameters TPM_RC_P + n counted after the handles).
+#define RC_ChangePPS_authHandle	(TPM_RC_H + TPM_RC_1)
 
 TPM_RC
 TPM2_ChangePPS(
